# Overview

A homemade tossing game: lay a string in a circle, set a big rock in the middle,
and toss small stones as close to it as you can, without touching it.

# Components

- 1x [[string]] — 3 m, thick, red
- 1x [[large rock]] — head-sized, the "heart"
- 6x [[small stone]] — palm-sized, two colours
- {4p} 2x [[small stone]] — extra pair, third colour
- 1x [[stick]] — to mark the throwing line

![How we set it up](media/layout.jpg)

# Setup

1. Lay the [[string]] in a circle on the ground, about 1 m across.
2. Put the [[large rock]] in the centre.
3. Mark a throwing line with the [[stick]], 4 big steps from the circle.
4. Hand out stones: {2p: 3 each | 3p: 2 each | 4p: 2 each, using the extra pair}.

# Play

- Take turns tossing one [[small stone]] from behind the line.
- ! A stone that touches the [[large rock]] is [[burnt]]: remove it.
- {2p} Alternate stones until all 6 are thrown.
- {3-4p} Go around clockwise until everyone has thrown all their stones.
- Each player has 20 seconds to throw. Slow players lose the stone.

# Scoring

! Closest stone to the rock that is still inside the circle: 3 points. Every other stone inside the circle: 1 point.

| Points to win        | 2p | 3p | 4p |
|----------------------|----|----|----|
| {-teams} Each player | 15 | 12 | 10 |
| {+teams} Each team   |    |    | 15 |

## Team play {+teams}

- {4p} Play in two teams of two, partners standing opposite.
- ! Team-mates' stones add up; scores are kept per team.
- Partners may knock each other's stones closer, but a stone pushed onto the [[large rock]] is [[burnt]] as usual.

# Glossary

Burnt
: A stone that touched the large rock; it is out of the round.
